snp3.6:47.1 starts: In your words, Nāga of nāgas, great hero,
snp3.6:47.2 starts: all devas—
# superseded: snp3.6:47.3 starts: including Nāradas and Pabbatas—
# superseded: snp3.6:47.4 starts: delight.
snp3.7:16.1 starts: A monk with skin resembling gold
snp3.7:16.2 starts: is admirable to look at,
snp3.7:16.3 starts: but what use is the contemplative state
snp3.7:16.4 starts: for you, so superlative in appearance?
snp3.8:4.1 starts: As clay vessels made by a potter
snp3.8:4.2 starts: all end up broken,
snp3.8:4.3 starts: so too life
snp3.8:4.4 starts: heads to death.
snp3.6:40.1 starts: Avoiding whatever action there is
snp3.6:40.2 starts: that ripens in suffering & stress
snp3.6:40.3 starts: one who goes about, comprehending,
snp3.6:40.4 starts: he has put an all-around end to
snp3.6:40.5 starts: name-&-form:
snp3.6:40.6 starts: He’s called a wanderer,
snp3.6:42.1 starts: “One Deeply Discerning,
snp3.6:42.2 starts: dependent on the teachings of contemplatives,
snp3.6:42.3 starts: dependent on perceptions
snp3.6:42.4 starts: & words of perceptions.
snp3.6:51.1 starts: As a lovely lotus
snp3.6:51.2 starts: is not smeared by water,
snp3.6:51.3 starts: you are not smeared
snp3.6:51.4 starts: by good or evil.
snp3.6:51.5 starts: Extend your feet, hero:
snp3.6:51.6 starts: Sabhiya venerates them,
snp3.7:18.1 starts: Noble warriors, feudal lords, & kings
snp3.7:18.2 starts: are your devotees.
snp3.7:18.3 starts: King of kings, monarch of human beings:
snp3.7:18.4 starts: Rule, Gotama!”
snp3.7:22.1 starts: The Buddha:
snp3.7:22.3 starts: the unexcelled Dhamma-wheel:
snp3.7:22.4 starts: Sāriputta keeps it rolling
snp3.7:22.5 starts: taking after the Tathāgata.
snp3.7:25.1 starts: I am one
snp3.7:25.2 starts: whose appearance in the world
snp3.7:25.3 starts: is hard often to gain:
snp3.7:25.4 starts: Rightly Self-Awakened,
snp3.8:2.1 starts: For there’s no way
snp3.8:2.2 starts: by which those who are born
snp3.8:2.3 starts: Beings are subject
snp3.8:2.4 starts: even when they attain
snp3.8:5.1 starts: Young & old
snp3.8:5.2 starts: wise & foolish:
snp3.8:5.3 starts: All
snp3.8:5.4 starts: all
snp3.8:9.1 starts: “You don’t know the path
snp3.8:9.2 starts: of his coming or going:
snp3.8:9.3 starts: seeing neither end,
snp3.8:9.4 starts: you lament in vain.”
snp3.8:10.1 starts: If, by lamenting,
snp3.8:10.2 starts: —confused,
snp3.8:10.3 starts: any use could be gained
snp3.8:10.4 starts: the prudent would do it as well.
